#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polynomial_remainder

#% text
# `polynomial_remainder(p, q, x)` gives the remainder of the division of `p` by `q` as polynomials in `x`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The remainder has lower degree in `x` than `q`; it is 0 when `q` divides `p`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polynomial_remainder(x^3 + 2*x + 1, x - 1, x)
#% output
#= 4

#% cell
polynomial_remainder(x^4 - 1, x^2 + 1, x)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
polynomial_remainder(x^2, 2*x + 1, x)
#% output
#= 1/4

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The remainder theorem: the remainder by `x - a` is `p(a)`:

#% cell
p = x^4 - 3*x + 2; [polynomial_remainder(p, x - 2, x), rewrite(p, x -> 2)]
#% output
#= [12, 12]

#% text
# Reducing powers modulo a minimal polynomial: `sqrt(2)^7` from `x^7` modulo `x^2 - 2`:

#% cell
polynomial_remainder(x^7, x^2 - 2, x)
#% output
#= 8*x

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `polynomial_quotient`, `polynomial_gcd`, `mod`
